<title>USA: ALPINE SKIING-LEAD TIMES AFTER FIRST RUN OF WORLD CUP SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-LEAD TIMES AFTER FIRST RUN OF WORLD CUP SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>MAMMOTH LAKES, California 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading</p>
<p>times after the first leg of a women's World Cup slalom at</p>
<p>Mammoth Mountain on Friday:</p>
<p>1. Sabine Egger (Austria) 37.72 seconds</p>
<p>2. Pernilla Wiberg (Sweden) 38.07</p>
<p>3. Deborah Compagnoni (Italy) 38.09</p>
<p>4. Lara Magoni (Italy) 38.28</p>
<p>5. Elfi Eder (Austria) 38.62</p>
<p>6. Karin Roten (Switzerland) 38.67</p>
<p>7. Anita Wachter (Austria) 38.72</p>
<p>8. Patricia Chauvet (France) 38.77</p>
<p>9. Trine Bakke (Norway) 39.08</p>
<p>10. Martina Accola (Switzerland) 39.21</p>
